cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these materials, please cite them as below."
title: "Absent Edges, Exp A: incomplete code-graph answers in a local Gemma 4 agent (code, protocols and paper materials)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Arjun Thilak R"
    affiliation: "Eros Innovation"
  - name: "Ramkumar MV"
    affiliation: "Eros Innovation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arjunthilak05/missing-callers-gemma4"
url: "https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rarjunthilak/absent-edges-expa-v1"
version: "1.0.0"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Code, preregistered protocols, frozen result files and paper materials of a preregistered omission probe:
  for a local Gemma 4 agent, does an offered code-graph tool get requested, does the agent recover a caller
  that a delivered caller list omits, and does it claim its own list is complete? 30 permissively licensed
  Python libraries, 750 targets with call-site truth, five answer conditions, and a hash-pinned number
  registry for every result in the paper.
keywords:
  - code graphs
  - software engineering agents
  - call graphs
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
  - Gemma 4
